Debug.Assert(OLD(_items.Length) + _size = _items.Length);
</code>

This assert statement is related to the comment that starts with "@@@" in the Insert method of the ArrayList class. This comment says: "@@@ last index of x does not decrease on inserting x in the array". This comment implies that when an element is inserted into the array, its length increases by one, but the index of the element does not change. This may cause confusion because it seems like the element's position has moved, but its index hasn't changed. The assert statement checks that the sum of the old length of the array (_items.Length) and the current size of the list (_size) is equal to the current length of the array. If the assertion fails, it means an element has been inserted into the array but the index of the element has not changed, indicating a problem with the code.
